// The grade-dev / grade-final job handler (server/jobs.ts PipelineHandlers.grade): everything a
// grading needs, read from the database and the blob store, then gradeEntry / regradeL1 / regradeL2,
// then the run row (record.ts). Returns the run to publish. And an agent/v1 grade's own two job
// handlers, grade-trial and grade-aggregate (PipelineHandlers.gradeTrial, gradeAggregate: `agent/v1`
// below).
//
//   live grades    once a final-phase grade run is stored (a grade's recordGrade, an agent/v1 run's fan-in, a
//                  scrape/v1 final heat's runs), finalGradeLanded records a live change on the competition's
//                  `phase` topic, kind `grade` (server/competitions/live-judging.ts openGradeLive: at most one
//                  per JUDGE_LIVE_MIN_GAP_MS a competition, one inside the gap at its end), so a page holding
//                  the live stream reads GET /live again and its judging's grades count moves; never failing
//                  the grade (what goes wrong is logged)
//   submission     snapshot_sha256 (readSnapshotIndex), house, submitted_as_house, baseline,
//                  pricing_rev. The score's `house` is the standings' (server/payouts/standings.ts
//                  standingsHouse): a house entry, or any other entry a house account
//                  submitted that is no baseline, so a house account's entry from a GitHub
//                  repository outside the house organizations is never prize-eligible, as the
//                  export's `house` says (payouts/onchain.ts resultEntriesOf); a regrade reads it alike
//   competition    its validated bundle (harness, limits, leaderboard, and the eligibility rules
//                  score.ts eligibilityRulesOf reads: min_authored_coverage,
//                  submission_rule.transcripts_required, prize_requires_beating_hold_cash, and
//                  whether it has a build meter); a program/v1 bundle's directory on disk
//   phase          dev | final, and its dataset (pumpfun-replay/v2, bars-replay/v1, clmm-replay/v1:
//                  every phase of a replay grades on one): the row is read here, its files by
//                  loadDataset (a chain log; default dataset.ts createDatasetLoader), loadBarsDataset
//                  (a bars window; default dataset.ts createBarsDatasetLoader) or loadClmmDataset (a
//                  clmm window; default dataset.ts createClmmDatasetLoader), the collector's formats,
//                  every hash verified against the manifest and the manifest against the row. A bars
//                  window that cannot replay the bundle's universe (a symbol it does not carry,
//                  another mint or interval), or a clmm window that cannot replay its pool (another
//                  pool, bars that are not its rows') or is too short for its blocks (under its
//                  phase's floor of whole ones of the harness's interval.block_hours, 28 on final and
//                  8 on dev: `ranked floor` below, harnesses.ts ClmmShortWindowError), can never
//                  grade it: a PermanentJobError
//   cost           usage_line rows (cost.ts) and every transcript_session row (its provenance, and
//                  whether it reports usage: a session that reports none leaves the cost unpriced);
//                  under a bundle with a build meter (build_meter) the entrant's metered_request rows
//                  in the competition through the submission's created_at, matched against those
//                  lines (entry-cost.ts, metered.ts: `metered` below)
//   metered        a fresh grade of an entry under a build meter first syncs every build key its
//                  entrant holds in the competition from masq through the submission's created_at
//                  (server/metering/sync.ts syncEntrantKeys, through deps.meter: the pipeline hands
//                  in the metering job's broker; by default the environment's masq,
//                  MAKEFUN_LLM_GATEWAY=masq), so every request its cost counts is stored before it is
//                  read. A MasqBrokerError there, or no masq to ask while the entrant holds a key still
//                  to sync, is the platform's and never the entry's: a retryable Error, nothing
//                  recorded. masq stamps a request when it ends (src/meter.ts recordRequest: ts is the
//                  clock at the request's last byte), so one ending after the receipt is never counted,
//                  and its row reaches masq's store through its ingest writer: within a second
//                  (src/ingest/ch-sink.ts CH_FLUSH_MS), but through a ClickHouse outage only once the
//                  store answers again (a retry backing off to 30 s, the rows spilled to disk after
//                  30 s and replayed, a handed-over slot's spill picked up within a minute), so a
//                  request at or before the receipt can be answered late. A final grade (the phase
//                  that places and pays) therefore prices only once masq has had CAP_GUARD_LOOKBACK_MS
//                  (server/metering/sync.ts: the hour the metering job's cap guard already reaches
//                  back for rows masq records late) past the receipt: sooner, the job sends itself
//                  again for then (METERED_SETTLE_SLACK_MS past it; meteredSettleJobId of the job,
//                  on its own queue, through deps.jobs: none is a retryable Error) and hands on
//                  nothing, nothing synced, run or recorded: it tells the caller so (the handler's
//                  `handedOn`), and the pipeline sends nothing after the job (server/jobs.ts
//                  PipelineHandlers.gradeHandedOn: no hindsight sweep, cluster scan, code heat or
//                  publish; the job sent again sends them once it grades). A dev grade prices at
//                  once, on what masq answers then: provisional, as a dev board is (no prize is
//                  paid on it), and a request masq records later counts in the entrant's next entry,
//                  never re-priced into this one. The grade keeps the list of the requests
//                  it counted (entry-cost.ts `the list`: Cost.metered.requests_sha256), and an L1 or
//                  L2 regrade prices from exactly the stored rows that list names and never calls
//                  masq, so a row stored since never moves it: it re-derives the cost the grade
//                  stored. A list it cannot read, or a row it names that is gone, refuses the regrade
//                  (PermanentJobError)
//   authorship     loadAuthorship (default loadStoredAuthorship: the authorship_summary row the
//                  ingest wrote under the submission's pricing_rev): a grade takes the newest
//                  algorithm version; a regrade the version its stored run's score names
//                  (storedAuthorshipVersion), so an entry ingested again under a newer algorithm
//                  still regrades byte for byte (none when the run was graded with none; a
//                  version no row holds is a PermanentJobError)
//
// Rules decided here:
//   runtime        main.ts at the snapshot root -> node22, main.py -> python3.13; neither, both, or
//                  one the competition does not accept fails the entry without running anything. A
//                  patch/v1 entry (a diff) names none: it runs on its plan's (harnesses.ts PATCH_RUNTIME)
//   seed           one per (competition, phase, dataset): phaseSeed below (a replay's dataset part
//                  its dataset row's sha256), the competition's part competitionSeedKey (its seed_key,
//                  pinned when first seeded, so a later bundle edit never moves it). It is hello.seed (the
//                  bot's to use) and the bootstrap's seed, so every entry of a phase is resampled
//                  alike. A bars phase that races live (racesLive: the ranking phase carrying a race,
//                  contracts/competition.ts raceOf), and a pump phase that races live on fail-key scheme
//                  server-secret/v1 (gradeTakesRaceSeed), is seeded as its race seeds every racer's hello,
//                  server/race/entries.ts raceSeed (phaseSeed with no dataset part: none is frozen while the
//                  race runs), so a bot that reads hello.seed answers its official grade as it answered live
//                  (a bars race's crosscheck holds; a pump race, raced under this seed's fail key too, trades
//                  as its grade does). A pump phase that races live on any other scheme (phase-secret+beacon/v1:
//                  a sealed-window final committed at its deadline, whose commitment holds every final run to
//                  the phase seed of its drawn window, server/chain/verify.ts checkCommittedFailKey) keeps its
//                  dataset part, its race's hello seed the race's own (server/race/runner.ts); every other
//                  phase keeps its dataset part, and a regrade the seed its run recorded
//   crosscheck     a grade run recorded on the phase a bundle races live (racesLive) holds the race to it as it
//                  lands, the phase's results published (crosscheckLandedGrade: server/race/crosscheck.ts
//                  crosscheckRace over this job's blob store, which compares nothing before finalized_at, then
//                  every racer not compared yet whose official run is scored), so a race an admin's finalize
//                  published as it queued the final grades is compared as they land, with no reader of /live
//                  waited on. It never fails the grade: the run is recorded first, and a racer whose action log
//                  could not be read, or a crosscheck that fails, is logged (deps.log) and left uncompared for the
//                  live snapshot's retry (server/routes/live/snapshot.ts FrameBoard.crosscheck). A regrade lands no
//                  official run (the crosscheck reads grade runs alone) and compares nothing
//   fail key       the pump replay's failed-tx draw's key (the bars and clmm replays draw nothing), one per phase too, so every entry of a phase meets the
//                  same draws, never sent to the bot, derived by the phase's scheme (phase.fail_key_scheme:
//                  phaseFailKey):
//                    server-secret/v1        failKeyFor, as before the schemes: on dev public (publicFailKey of
//                                            the phase seed, which a kit reproduces), on final HKDF-SHA256 of the
//                                            server secret (deps.failKeySecret: config.betterAuthSecret) over the
//                                            phase seed
//                    phase-secret+beacon/v1  a final phase committed at its deadline: committedFailKey
//                                            (server/chain/deadline-commitment.ts) of the phase's own secret
//                                            (phase.fail_key_secret), the phase seed and the drand signature of the
//                                            sealed window's beacon round. The signature is the draw record's
//                                            (<deps.sealedDir>/<slug>/draw.json, verified against the competition
//                                            directory's sealed-window.yaml: verifyDrawRecord), taken only while
//                                            the phase's deadline commitment holds it: the document hashes to its
//                                            stored sha256, is this competition's sealed pool, fixed the secret's
//                                            sha256 and names the sidecar the draw was made for, its round and its
//                                            chain; and the drawn masked window is the phase's dataset. A phase
//                                            with no secret, no draw record that verifies, or one its commitment
//                                            does not name is a FailKeyUnavailableError: the job retries, the
//                                            admins are paged (at most once an hour per phase and reason in a
//                                            process: failKeyPager), and the server secret is never read instead
//                  The run keeps the key it was graded with (GradeOutcome.fail_key); a regrade reuses the stored
//                  run's when the row has one, else derives it again from the stored seed, by the phase's scheme
//   final window   the latest receipt server_time among the competition's submissions (null on dev)
//   instance       an instance-drawn program/v1 bundle (harness.generator) grades on a drawn instance
//                  under the sealed directory (deps.sealedDir; server/competitions/load.ts lays it out),
//                  never on data of its own (phaseInstance): its instance.yaml (in the competition
//                  directory) read and checked against the stored bundle; the dev phase on the practice
//                  instance, practice/{input,reference}, each tree digesting to the sidecar's practice
//                  digest; the final phase on scored-<k>/ of the newest instance-draw-<k>.json, the
//                  whole draw chain verified from the sidecar and drand (verifyInstanceDraws) and the
//                  instance's trees digesting to the record's (its programDataSha256 the record's
//                  instance_sha256). No draw record yet, no final grading yet: the grade waits for the
//                  draw (`not drawn` below). The phase seed's dataset part is
//                  the instance's digest (programDataSha256 of its two directories: the run's
//                  dataset_sha256), so a redraw seeds anew and a regrade of a run on another draw is
//                  refused (regrade.ts compares dataset_sha256). The scorer stays the bundle's own.
//   pack           a pack program/v1 bundle (harness.pack: a code bounty's) grades each phase on its
//                  pack's trees, never on data of its own (phasePackTrees): the dev phase on pack.dev,
//                  the final phase on pack.final, each tree materialized read-only from the blob store
//                  into <work root>/pack-trees/<digest>/ and re-hashed against its digest before every
//                  use (server/competitions/load.ts packTreeDir: a tree the store lacks is taken from a
//                  house pack competition's own copy, competitions/<slug>/pack/, once it re-hashes). Its
//                  programs are read from load.ts programCompetitionDir (competitions/code-tests-01, the
//                  house tests scorer, for a sponsored one with no directory of its own), its scorer
//                  directory re-hashed against the harness's scorer_sha256 first. A tree in neither
//                  place, or a scorer that does not re-hash, is a PermanentJobError. The phase seed's
//                  dataset part is the run's dataset digest (programDataSha256 of the two trees). Under
//                  cases 'per-file' the entry runs once per case (grader/program.ts), and under a gate
//                  the score carries performance.passed (grader/score.ts)
//   patch/v1       a patch/v1 bundle (contracts/patch.ts) grades each phase on the bounty's sealed base tree
//                  (repo.base_tree_sha256) and the phase's tree (pack.dev on dev, pack.final on final), never
//                  on data of its own (patchPhaseSetup): each materialized read-only from the blob store
//                  into <work root>/patch-base/<digest>/ and <work root>/patch-phase/<digest>/ and re-verified
//                  against its index on every use (patch/execute.ts patchTreeDir), the phase's lists read
//                  from its lists.json. A tree the store does not hold, or lists that do not read, is a
//                  PlatformFaultError (NO_PATCH_TREES_MESSAGE), as is a grade on the k8s sandbox, whose
//                  pods run no repository image. The phase seed's dataset part is the phase tree's digest
//                  (the run's dataset_sha256). No test log is kept, on either phase
//   referral/v1    a referral/v1 entry (contracts/competition.ts ReferralHarness) is checked, never run: its score is
//                  the verified sign-ups its submitter brought, read from the referral contest's facts
//                  (server/referrals/contest.ts verifiedSignupCountsOf and undecidedContestReferralsOf) inside
//                  [competition.opens_at, competition.deadline], recorded as the run's action log
//                  (grader/score.ts ReferralActionLog: each sign-up, counted or not, and why) and scored from that log
//                  alone (buildScore counts its counted sign-ups). No sandbox, runtime, dataset, snapshot file, entry
//                  secret or pod is read or held; a snapshot is still required (the entry set takes only snapshotted
//                  entries). A final grade with a still-undecided sign-up hands itself on for REFERRAL_GRADE_RESEND_MS
//                  while the phase has time left, and at its end counts what is decided (an undecided one never
//                  counts); a dev grade counts at once and the referral-contest sweep sends it afresh when the count
//                  moves. Its L1 regrade re-scores the stored log; its L2 is refused (a count is the facts at the
//                  grade's read)
//   k8s data       on the k8s sandbox (MAKEFUN_SANDBOX=k8s) every host path a sandbox pod is staged from or
//                  collected into lies under the data root (sandbox/k8s.ts checkUnderDataRoot: no sandbox pod
//                  mounts the claim, every tree is copied over its exec into the pod's own emptyDirs, and a
//                  spec names no tree of the grader's outside that root), so a program/v1 grade's setup has
//                  every tree its pods are staged from that lies outside MAKEFUN_K8S_DATA_ROOT copied under
//                  it before any pod is made (stageProgramSetup): a bundle's own input/, reference/ and
//                  scorer directory, read from the image's competitions/<slug>/, are copied once to
//                  <data root>/bundle-trees/<slug>/<digest>/<path in the bundle>, read-only, each re-hashed
//                  against the digest its harness seals it to before every use (sandbox/bundle-trees.ts),
//                  and staged into the pods from there. An instance's trees under the sealed directory and
//                  a pack's under the work root lie under the data root already and are staged from where
//                  they are. The copies are byte for byte, so the run's dataset and scorer digests are the
//                  image's. A tree the image does not hold as sealed is a PlatformFaultError. The same holds
//                  for the bundle trees an agent/v1 trial and a scrape/v1 scorer are staged from: an
//                  agent/v1 setup has its env directory and its scorer directory copied as env_sha256 and
//                  scorer_sha256 (stageAgentSetup) before any pass of a trial job and before an agent
//                  regrade, and a scrape/v1 scorer setup its scorer directory as scorer_sha256
//                  (stageScrapeScorerSetup) before a heat and before an L1 regrade (agentSetupFor,
//                  scrapeScorerSetupFor: the setup as it is off the k8s sandbox). Their instances (sealed
//                  directory), the forwarder bundles and every scratch (work root) lie under the data root
//                  already. The docker and process drivers mount the image's paths as before
//   size          a program/v1 bundle naming a size count (harness.size: a Smallest code bounty's) scores
//                  every grade and regrade with the entry's code size (grader/size.ts codeSize) over the
//                  submission's snapshot index, less the competition's starter where the entry kept it
//                  unchanged: competitions/<slug>/starter/ as its kit hands it out
//                  (server/routes/competitions/kit.ts starterFiles; deps.starter, competitionStarter),
//                  so grade-local, counting over the kit.json listing, gives the same bytes. Counted once
//                  per job, before anything runs, and handed to gradeEntry, regradeL1 and regradeL2
//                  alike (GradeRequest.size, RegradeL1Request.size)
//   stopping       a grade stops once its job attempt's signal aborts (JobContext.signal: pg-boss gave the
//                  attempt up at its expiry, or the workers stop): gradeEntry kills the program running and
//                  starts none after it (grade.ts `Stopping`: a run per case stops between cases), a dev
//                  grade's timing likewise, and the job records no run (the signal is read again before the
//                  run row is written) and throws the signal's reason, no PermanentJobError: the retry
//                  grades afresh, not beside an attempt still running. A regrade stops alike: regradeL1's
//                  scorer, regradeL2's re-execution and scorer (regrade.ts `stopping`), and an agent/v1 L2's
//                  replays. An agent/v1 L1 and a scrape/v1 L1 take no signal and run to their end. No regrade
//                  records anything once the signal has aborted
//   entry          an entry graded as one execution (pumpfun-replay/v2, bars-replay/v1, clmm-replay/v1,
//   secrets        program/v1) runs with its entrant's env-lane entry secrets: a grade reads the account's
//                  active ones in the competition (activeEnvSecrets: server/secrets/store.ts
//                  sealedEntrySecretsFor, the env lane's alone: no provider-lane value ever reaches a sandbox
//                  but an agent/v1 forwarder, and sandbox/types.ts checkSandboxSecrets refuses one besides) and
//                  opens each with the grader's private keys (GradeWorkerDeps.entrySecrets.seal, default the
//                  environment's), before anything runs; none pushed: none, and no key read. They ride the
//                  entry's SnapshotSource (grade.ts SnapshotSource.secrets), so both of the grade's executions,
//                  every case of a run per case, every practice window of an eras run and a dev grade's
//                  provisional timing run the entry with the same values; the scorer never. One this grader
//                  cannot open (no private key here, a seal it lacks, a record that does not open) HOLDS the
//                  grade, which never fails the entry for it, the fault being the platform's key
//                  configuration and never the entrant's: nothing of the entry runs, no run is recorded, and
//                  the job throws EntrySecretsUnopenedError (its message opening
//                  ENTRY_SECRETS_UNOPENED_HOLD_REASON as snapshot.ts EntrySecretsHeldError's does, then each
//                  secret that did not open by NAME and row, and why; never a value), a retryable Error that
//                  pg-boss retries (each held attempt logged). On the job's LAST attempt (isLastAttempt) the
//                  handler throws EntrySecretsHeldFault instead, a PlatformFaultError, so the pipeline's grade
//                  stage never fails the entry: it puts it back to the status that attempt found, its error
//                  untouched (server/pipeline/index.ts; after an earlier held attempt that is the `running`
//                  the stage set), and the job dead-letters, paged once (`dead grade job` below: the page
//                  names the keys to mount and the resend, which grades it with them once a process holding
//                  them runs it). A regrade held so (an L2's recorded rows, an agent/v1 L2's) throws the same
//                  retryable error, its last attempt paged alike. The run records the rows by id
//                  (run.entry_secret_ids, record.ts RunSecrets; an eras run from its start). A final-phase run
//                  records them under its entrant's account lock (recordWithSecretsHeld: FOR SHARE on the user
//                  row, which a secret's push and delete take FOR NO KEY UPDATE), in the transaction that
//                  writes it, and only while every one of them still holds its ciphertext: a delete or replace
//                  after it then sees the run and keeps the row sealed for the challenge's L2 (server/secrets/
//                  store.ts finalRecorded), and one that erased a row while the grade ran leaves no run to
//                  record (a retryable Error naming it by NAME: the retry grades with the secrets as they
//                  stand), so no final run of these ever names a row its challenge re-run cannot open (a
//                  scrape/v1 run has no re-run: below). An agent/v1 final pass claims its trial alike (its
//                  env-lane rows checked in the claim's transaction: one erased since its pass opened it
//                  sends the pass round again, nothing claimed). Its stderr and error are masked of every
//                  form of every value (grade.ts executeOnce, record.ts putStderr). Its action log and, on
//                  program/v1, every output file it lists are scanned after the grade, never masked (they
//                  are scored byte for byte: secretHitsOfRun): a hit
//                  flags the run SECRET_IN_OUTPUT_FLAG (beside its score's flags, never in them: regrade.ts
//                  RUN_ONLY_FLAGS) with a SECRET_IN_OUTPUT_ACTION row (subject the run; data run_id and hits,
//                  each a NAME and a file: ACTION_LOG_SCAN_FILE, `output/<path>`, an eras window's under its
//                  key), in the transaction that records it. An L2 re-opens exactly the rows the run recorded
//                  (recordedEnvSecrets: retained rows included) and runs with them; once one is erased
//                  (replaced, deleted or purged) it is refused unexecuted (regrade.ts ENTRY_SECRETS_ERASED,
//                  recorded as a failed regrade_l2 run flagged so) and the run's L1, which needs no secret,
//                  stands. An agent/v1 L2 re-opens each replayed trial's (run_trial.entry_secret_ids, the env
//                  lane's) alike (AgentRegradeL2Request.trialSecrets). A code heat times each field entry with
//                  the rows its graded run recorded, re-opened (one erased since is left out, by NAME in the
//                  log: its timed outputs then show whether it mattered). A scrape/v1 heat (runScrapeHeatFor)
//                  opens every entrant's active ones before anything of the heat is made and runs each
//                  entrant's every trial with its own (grader/scrape/heat.ts, trial.ts: their values on the
//                  house launcher's stdin, never in a file; the cassette, the scrape answer key, its bodies
//                  and the launcher's tails masked of every form; /output scanned); the heat's reference read,
//                  the house's, runs with none, and so does every house entry (housePaysEntryLane: a house
//                  entry or a baseline, as an agent/v1 pass's), its account's secrets never read or opened.
//                  Each recorded run records its rows (run.entry_secret_ids), its error masked, and a form in
//                  its trials' /output (heat.ts ScrapeHeatRun.secret_hits, every attempt's) or its action log
//                  flags it SECRET_IN_OUTPUT_FLAG with one SECRET_IN_OUTPUT_ACTION row, all in the transaction
//                  that records the heat's runs (record.ts recordScrapeRuns, ScrapeRunRecord's RunSecrets). It
//                  records them without a final-phase grade's erased-row check (recordWithSecretsHeld):
//                  nothing runs a scrape entry with its recorded rows again (its L2 is refused, and neither a
//                  hindsight audit nor a dev stress runs one), and the check would let one entrant's delete
//                  send the whole final heat round again. A hindsight audit's surrogate runs and a dev
//                  stress's copies (grader/dev-stress.ts) re-open exactly the rows the run they stand for
//                  recorded, as an L2 does (recordedEnvSecrets), and run with them, masked alike
//                  (grader/hindsight-audit.ts runOnWindow): one erased since refuses the audit or the stress
//                  for good (a PermanentJobError naming it by NAME; a dead audit is paged, its verdict given by
//                  hand), one this grader cannot open retries it. A live race's racer gets none, nor does a
//                  judge, or the scorer
//   agent/v1      an agent entry grades as K trials (contracts/agent.ts), each a LIVE pass (its model
//                  calls metered and recorded in a cassette: a house-paid entry's on a masq key of the
//                  pass's own, an entrant's on its own keys, `entry lane` below) and, on the final phase, a
//                  REPLAY of it (grader/agent.ts runTrial; a dev trial runs once: `practice once` below),
//                  on the phase's instances (agentPhaseTrials,
//                  read from the trials sidecar instance.yaml and the sealed directory as `instance`
//                  reads a program/v1 bundle's): the dev phase one trial, on practice trial 0; the final
//                  phase every trial of the newest scored draw. Three jobs carry it (server/jobs.ts):
//     grade        startAgentRun: the run's row (record.ts startRun, status running, under the id
//                  agentRunId derives from the grade job, so a retry finds it) and its K run_trial rows
//                  (a staged final's trial 0 alone: `staged final` below; pending, each tagged with its place in the queue: record.ts `queue tags`), one
//                  grade-trial job per trial for live pass 1 (gradeTrialJobId, at gradeTrialPriority of
//                  its tag: contests share the slots, an entrant's trials queue behind its own, and trial
//                  0 of every entry of a final runs first) and the fan-in's first job. It
//                  publishes nothing. The run's dataset_sha256 is agentDatasetSha256 of its instances,
//                  its seed the phase seed over it; an entry that selects no runtime fails at once
//     grade-trial  createAgentTrialHandler moves one trial on from where its row stands, as far as the
//                  job's pass reaches; every move is written only while the row is still where it was
//                  read (record.ts moveTrial), so of two attempts on one trial one moves it:
//                    pending / void   live pass `pass` (its key minted, then the row claimed:
//                                     live_running, attempt = pass, the void's record cleared into
//                                     voided spend; an entrant's pass, which mints no key for its
//                                     entry lane, claims it as its house key comes back, or with no
//                                     target as it sets out: `entry lane` below), unscored; ends
//                                     live_done, timeout (0 on every column, done), or void. Its
//                                     key retired, the run takes the
//                                     flags its spend read sets (masqRunFlags: masq.ts's
//                                     gateway_spend_mismatch on a settled figure the meter disagrees
//                                     with, GATEWAY_SPEND_UNSETTLED_FLAG on one that never settled),
//                                     for admins only and never a score; on a house clock
//                                     (grader/house-clock.ts, the setup's `competition` its slug),
//                                     each pass, its replay's too, flags the run with the credit it
//                                     ran on (houseClockRunFlags), never a score either
//                    void             a series of AGENT_SERIES_PASSES live passes from the job's
//                                     first_pass: a void before its last sends the next pass its
//                                     own job (after AGENT_VOID_RERUN_DELAY_MS; an upstream_errors
//                                     void's after 5, then 10 minutes, agentVoidRerunDelayMs, so a
//                                     series outlasts a burst) on the same instance
//                                     with a fresh key; the last holds the trial. A pass cut off
//                                     (INTERRUPTED_VOID_REASON) spends none of it (`cut off` below)
//                    live_running     this job's pass cut off (the attempt that ran it stopped or
//                                     expired, or its grader died): what it left running removed
//                                     (`dead grader` below), then a void (INTERRUPTED_VOID_REASON),
//                                     its key retired, what masq metered on it counted as voided spend
//                                     (a figure that never settled flags the run
//                                     GATEWAY_SPEND_UNSETTLED_FLAG as a live pass's does)
//                    live_done        the export scored by the bundle's scorer (agent.ts
//                                     scoreTrialWithChecks; points checked as aggregateTrials counts
//                                     them), the per-check rows it wrote beside them kept with the
//                                     score (`checks` below), then the replay: finished or
//                                     nondeterministic, done. A recorded live pass never runs again,
//                                     and a scored one goes straight to its replay, or on the dev
//                                     phase straight to finished (`practice once` below)
//                    replaying        a replay cut off (no end on record): replayed again (it spends
//                                     nothing), what the cut-off one left running removed first
//                                     (`dead grader` below); one that met a fault records its end
//                                     (replay_finished_at, still replaying) and is retried as a fault
//                  cut off      a grader restart (a deploy, a rollout) cuts off every pass it runs, which is
//                               the platform's doing, never the entry's: a live pass voided
//                               INTERRUPTED_VOID_REASON is re-run spending no pass of its series (its
//                               next pass's job carries first_pass + 1, so the series counts the same
//                               passes), and a replay found cut off replays again. Each counts toward
//                               AGENT_INTERRUPTED_RERUNS in a row instead, on the row's error (a
//                               live void's words end `cut off <n> times in a row` from the second on,
//                               a replay's from its first: liveCutOffRun, replayCutOffRun); the
//                               AGENT_INTERRUPTED_RERUNS-th in a row holds the trial under
//                               INTERRUPTED_VOID_REASON, so one that kills its grader every time cannot
//                               loop. A job whose last attempt dies with the trial cut off is no fault
//                               either: the fan-in sends its pass's job again (`held` below). Those
//                               words, a void's and a hold's, stand on the row only until a pass ends
//                               otherwise: a live pass that ends live_done or timeout, and a replay that
//                               ends finished or nondeterministic, records its own ending (trialEnding:
//                               no void reason, and no error but a nondeterministic replay's fault), so
//                               no earlier attempt's fault outlives it; their history is the grader's
//                               log, the voided spend, the run's flags and a re-queue's audit row
//                  practice once  a dev-phase trial runs once (the owner, 2026-11-11: "for non-final
//                               grading we don't need to be so redundant"): its live pass recorded and
//                               scored, the trial is finished with no replay (replay_started_at and
//                               replay_finished_at stay null; server/db/schema.ts run_trial_replayed lets
//                               only a finished trial end so), and its run is flagged replay_skipped
//                               (regrade.ts REPLAY_SKIPPED_FLAG) in the same transaction. Nothing else of
//                               the live pass changes: its key minted and retired, its spend settled, its
//                               cassette, env log, state and outputs stored as before, so an L1 regrade and
//                               the public verification read all they read; an L2 regrade replays it there
//                               for the first time (regrade.ts `L2`). The replay was the half of a dev
//                               grade that told only whether it was nondeterministic (measured on
//                               production, 2026-11-11: 38-44% of a tiny-chess-01 trial's grading time, 27% of all
//                               trial slot-time); every final-phase trial still replays, as before. A dev
//                               trial found replaying (claimed by a release from before) replays to its end
//                               as before. The fan-in counts its executions as its live passes alone; the
//                               run's result carries no nondeterministic flag (no replay differed, as none ran:
//                               agent-score.ts agentDeterministic), so it ranks, and the flag tells every reader
//                               that no replay checked it (server/routes/archive/entry.ts agentTrialsOf)
//                  re-drawn     a dev trial's row names the practice instance it was made on (run_trial instance_sha256
//                  practice     and instance_ref, practice/trial-0), its run the dataset_sha256 and seed over it, and its
//                               limits are the bundle's as its job reads it; the release's practice draw re-draws
//                               practice/ IN PLACE once the committed instance.yaml changes (server/competitions/
//                               practice-draw.ts). So a queued trial never plays an old instance under a new bundle's
//                               limits, nor voids `instance` three times and is held: before a dev pass sets out from
//                               pending or void, when instance.yaml (read unverified, a hint alone) or the tree says the
//                               row's instance may not be the one drawn, the phase's practice trial is read as
//                               startAgentRun reads it (agentPhaseTrials). Not drawn yet (InstanceNotDrawnError:
//                               practice/ missing, or not what instance.yaml commits to): no pass runs, nothing is marked,
//                               spent or paged; the job is sent again for the next PRACTICE_REDRAW_RECHECK_MS slot, its
//                               queue tag kept as a fault's, and the competition's practice-draw job sent (server/jobs.ts
//                               sendPracticeDraw). Drawn as another instance: the trial RE-POINTED in one transaction (its
//                               instance_sha256 and instance_ref the current trial's while the row is where it was read,
//                               its run's dataset_sha256 and seed startAgentRun's for the current draw while the run runs
//                               and no trial of it holds a recorded pass), one line logged naming both digests, and the
//                               pass runs on the current instance. A recorded live pass found unscored on a tree that no
//                               longer digests to its instance (re-drawn while it ran, or a trial held `scorer` or
//                               `instance` by a release before and re-queued) is voided INSTANCE_REDRAWN_VOID_REASON,
//                               spending no pass of its series as a cut-off pass does (its spend voided spend as any
//                               void's), and re-run, re-pointed as it sets out. A final's trials (its scored draw is never
//                               re-drawn), a dev trial whose instance is the one drawn, and every trial of a competition
//                               directory with no instance.yaml (no draw committed there to re-point to) run as above.
//                               A release that re-draws a practice instance ships the new instance.yaml in its image
//                               at its deploy, while the stored bundle changes only at its seed (minutes later, or hours
//                               if a seed is stopped): between the two the instance.yaml a new grader reads was drawn by
//                               another generator than the stored bundle seals. On the dev phase that is an
//                               InstanceNotDrawnError naming instance.yaml (agentPhaseTrials, releaseWindowError),
//                               never a PermanentJobError: a new dev grade waits in the grade stage as for a practice
//                               tree (its path no practice tree's, so it sends no draw, and it pages once past its
//                               wait), and a queued dev trial waits here (practiceNotDrawn), so no entry is failed or
//                               held, and no pass plays the old instance under the old wall beside the new house
//                               clock row. The seed mends it: the trial then waits for the re-draw if practice/ is not
//                               drawn yet, and runs re-pointed on the new instance under the new bundle. A final's
//                               instance.yaml that is not its stored bundle's still fails for good. A pass in flight
//                               when the tree is due a re-draw (a draining grader of the release before, which scores
//                               it against reference/ under the row's path) is not drawn under: the practice-draw job
//                               waits for it (server/pipeline/index.ts deferringPracticeDraw). Nor is a tree re-drawn
//                               in the release window itself, whatever is in flight (practiceReleaseWindow): until the
//                               seed, graders of the release before may still be claiming trials mid-rollout and
//                               starting passes on the old tree, so the draw waits for the seed, which runs only once
//                               every one of them is draining (claiming nothing), and then for their passes in flight
//                  staged final a final phase whose bundle stages it (contracts/competition.ts stagedFinalOf:
//                               stagedFinalRun; every other phase and bundle grades as above, byte for byte):
//                               every entry runs the draw's trial 0 alone, and only the contenders go on to
//                               all K. startAgentRun makes the run's trial 0 alone and sends its job; the
//                               run's dataset_sha256 is still agentDatasetSha256 of the WHOLE draw, which a
//                               regrade and the final kit compare it to. Trial 0's live pass scored, the
//                               phase's cut is read afresh (phase.cut_decided_at, cut_line_points: the run's
//                               context read the phase as the job began, a live pass ago). Undecided, the
//                               trial PARKS at live_done (the outcome `parked`): its queue tag deferred
//                               (record.ts deferTrialQueueTag, so a field of parked trials counts in no
//                               contest's n_c), the cut read once more (a decision between the two finds it
//                               still where its wake takes it from), and the phase's final-cut job poked
//                               under this minute's id (server/jobs.ts sendFinalCut, finalCutWaitJobId),
//                               nothing else written; the cut job wakes it once it decides. Decided, its
//                               verdict against the stored line (server/grading/final-cut.ts cutVerdictOf,
//                               on the points cutPointsOf reads of the one trial with the entry's facts, as
//                               the fan-in will score it): `cut` ends the trial as `practice once` does
//                               (finished, no replay, the run flagged replay_skipped in the same
//                               transaction, the fan-in told), so its one trial is all it is scored on;
//                               `contender` makes sure trials 1 to K-1 exist (record.ts insertTrials, which
//                               keeps the rows the cut job made on its contenders' line, their tags with
//                               them; a late contender's join its final's line) and sends each one's job for
//                               live pass 1 under its stable id (gradeTrialJobId pass 1, as the cut job
//                               sends it; a tag past MAX_GRADE_TRIAL_QUEUE_TAG at the cap's priority,
//                               logged, never a throw that strands a contender), then replays trial 0 as
//                               any final trial. A run measured after the decision (a late run, a held
//                               first trial an admin re-queued, which waits for an admin as any held trial)
//                               is judged against the stored line the same way and displaces nobody. A
//                               first trial that ran out of its wall is done already: undecided, it pokes
//                               the cut too; decided, a house entry's run (a contender whatever it scored)
//                               gets its later trials there, and an entrant's is cut. The fan-in finishes a
//                               staged final's run only once the cut is decided: a cut run on its one
//                               trial, a contender once all K of its trials exist and are done; until then
//                               it waits as on an open trial, and a parked first trial is never held for
//                               its dead job (its last job ended as it parked). The score is the fan-in's
//                               as ever (aggregateTrials over the listed trials): a cut run's lists one
//                               trial, its interval's bounds null.
//                               Stages: a final that names earlier `cuts` (StagedFinalT.cuts) makes several
//                               cuts (server/grading/final-cut.ts finalCutsOf: cut 0 after trial 0, each
//                               later one at the instances the cut before sent its survivors to, the last
//                               sending the finalists on to all K), and everything above keyed on trial 0
//                               widens to every qualifying trial, those under the last cut's position
//                               (stagedQualifyingTrials); with none, every path, job id, queue tag and score
//                               byte is the one-cut final's above. Each qualifying trial's live pass scored,
//                               the run's fate is read afresh (stagedFateOf: cut 0 off the phase, each later
//                               cut off its phase_cut row, and runFateOf over the run's trials measured as
//                               trial 0 is above, each cut judging the run's total over its first `at` trials
//                               once all are measured, against its stored line). Waiting (a cut undecided, or
//                               the run through a cut with its next stage not all measured), the trial PARKS
//                               as trial 0 does, its tag deferred and the fate read once more; a run through
//                               a cut gets that cut's next stage (trials `at` to `to` - 1) made where it is not
//                               (insertTrials, a no-op where the cut job made them on its stage's line) and
//                               their pass-1 jobs sent under gradeTrialJobId pass 1; the final-cut job is
//                               poked under this minute's id while the cut it waits on is undecided. Cut at a
//                               cut, the trial ends as `practice once` does (the run flagged replay_skipped in
//                               the same transaction, the fan-in told: no trial of a stopped run is replayed),
//                               and the run's other parked trials are woken under the cut's key
//                               (stagedWakeKey: `cut:<c>:<decided ms>`, cut 0's `cut:<decided ms>`, the cut
//                               job's own), whose handlers end them the same way. A finalist's remaining
//                               trials are made and sent, its other parked trials woken, and it REPLAYS, as
//                               every trial of a finalist does, the ones first run live only included; its
//                               own trials (index at the last cut's position and up) replay as any final
//                               trial. A qualifying trial at its wall is done already and pokes the cut
//                               while the cut it waits on is undecided; decided, it never goes on (a house
//                               entry's does), and its run's parked trials are woken as above. A run measured
//                               after a cut was decided is judged through each stored line in turn, displacing
//                               nobody. The fan-in finishes such a run once it is cut at some cut with every
//                               trial ended, or a finalist with all K done (final-cut.ts stagedRunOf over its
//                               fate); otherwise it waits as on an open trial, and it holds no parked
//                               qualifying trial of a run whose fate still waits for its dead job
//                  brief       a live pass copies the entry's brief as grader/agent.ts trialBriefSource
//                               picks it, handed the entry's baseline flag (submission.baseline): a house
//                               baseline on an instance holding reference/baseline-prompt.txt reads that,
//                               every other pass input/prompt.txt. The row records what the pass copied
//                               (run_trial prompt_sha256, baseline_prompt), and the replay hands runTrial
//                               that recorded choice, never the flag as it stands then: an admin may flip
//                               the flag between the two (no regrade is queued on a flip), and a replay on
//                               the other brief would miss its cassette, a false state_mismatch. A row
//                               recorded before the choice was replays on the flag. A replay that copied
//                               other bytes than its live pass recorded is a harness fault (replay_brief),
//                               never a verdict on the entry. The fan-in names each trial's prompt_sha256
//                               in the trials manifest, which an L2 regrade replays by (regrade.ts)
//                  checks       a scorer that writes per-check rows beside scores.json (program-scores.ts
//                               checks.json) has them kept on the trial's row with its score (run_trial
//                               checks, canonical JSON), or, when it wrote a malformed checks.json, why it
//                               was dropped (checks_issue: harnesses.ts scoreProgramBreakdown), the score
//                               standing as without it: a breakdown never fails a trial. The fan-in makes
//                               the run's checks trace of them (`grade-aggregate` below)
//                  dead grader  a grader that dies mid-pass leaves the pass's containers running on
//                               its network, and its scratch under the work root. Every pass of a
//                               trial names the trial's owner (trialOwner, `<run id>.<trial index>`;
//                               grader/agent.ts RunTrialOptions.owner), which labels its network
//                               makefun.trial=<owner>; before a pass makes its own network, and
//                               before a cut-off live pass is voided, every network carrying that
//                               label and each grader container on one are removed (network.ts
//                               reapTrial, through sandboxReap and runTrial's onReap) and logged by
//                               name (reapLine). Its scratch (the snapshot and the pass's own
//                               directory, and its scorer's) is named for the owner too,
//                               `<work root>/trial-<owner>-XXXXXX` (TRIAL_SCRATCH_PREFIX, regrade.ts
//                               ownedScratch); once a pass holds its trial (a live pass's claim,
//                               the replay's, a cut-off pass voided) every other directory so named
//                               is removed (regrade.ts reapScratch) and logged by path
//                               (scratchReapLine). A trial's passes run one at a time, each once
//                               its row is claimed for it, so what carries its owner then is a dead
//                               pass's; another trial's carries another owner. A pass looks only in
//                               its own process's work root (AgentTrialDeps.workRoot; an agent/v1
//                               regrade in GradeWorkerDeps.workRoot alike), and the pipeline's is
//                               the server's own across restarts (server/pipeline/index.ts
//                               startWorkers: config.workRoot, MAKEFUN_WORK_ROOT, default
//                               .data/work), so the grader that resumes a dead one's trial looks
//                               where it left its scratch. What no resumed pass comes back for the
//                               workers' start removes (server/pipeline/index.ts sweepDeadWork),
//                               and only once all three hold (removeIfDead): no active job on the
//                               start's database holds its owner, no one has touched it for six
//                               hours (its newest change, its own or a direct entry's, older than
//                               network.ts STALE_AFTER_MS), and no live process holds it open or as
//                               its cwd (processesHolding). A live pass's never ages so: ownedScratch
//                               hands every owned scratch out with a heartbeat, its `.alive`
//                               rewritten every ten minutes until the pass removes it (grade.ts
//                               keepScratchAlive), so a pass on another database sharing the work
//                               root keeps its scratch even where its containers' processes cannot be
//                               seen (the docker driver's). One younger, held or not to be asked
//                               about is kept and logged: a job on another database sharing the
//                               work root, or a run handed no job, may still work in it. A root no
//                               successor shares (a hand-built config's fresh per-process one, a
//                               test process's) is never looked in by the next process: only the
//                               opt-in sweep of per-process roots (MAKEFUN_SWEEP_PROCESS_WORK_ROOTS)
//                               removes it, once six hours still and held by no process
//                  entry lane   who pays the entry's own model calls (housePaysEntryLane). The house,
//                               for a house entry (submission.house), an entry a house account
//                               submitted (submitted_as_house) or a baseline: its live pass runs on a
//                               masq key of its own (grader/agent.ts TrialUpstream `masq`), minted
//                               before the claim. Never for an entrant's entry (the owner's rule: house
//                               money never pays an entrant's model calls): its live pass runs its entry
//                               lane on the entrant's own keys (agent.ts EntrantTrialUpstream `provider`;
//                               `entry secrets` below) and mints no masq key for it (masq_key_id stays
//                               null), the trial recorded entry_credential entrant with the entry_secret
//                               rows it ran with, both lanes (entry_secret_ids, a list exactly when the
//                               credential is entrant). An entrant with no provider key runs
//                               model-free (entrantKeysOf, the keys none): the forwarder answers each of
//                               its model calls itself, a 401 naming the entry secret that carries a key
//                               and how to push it (gateway/upstream.ts noProviderKeyMessage; with no
//                               seal public key on this deployment, so that a push answers 503, its words
//                               say pushing is not open here yet and name no command: `entry secrets`
//                               below), recorded in the cassette, sent
//                               nowhere and never counted toward a void (credential entrant: gateway/meter.ts), so the pass
//                               ends live_done and is scored and replayed as any other (no provider-lane
//                               id among entry_secret_ids). On the entrant's keys the same holds of a 401, 402, 403, 407 or
//                               429 its provider answers mid-pass (a key revoked, out of credit or rate
//                               limited is the entrant's, scored as the entry met it), while a 5xx, a 529
//                               or a reset still voids the pass and re-runs it. With a target its house
//                               lane still runs on a masq key (role house), and that key's mint claims the
//                               trial (house_masq_key_id), so a refused admin key still marks nothing; with
//                               none, nothing is minted and the trial is claimed as the pass sets out. Its
//                               entry lane spends no house money: what an entrant's pass spent
//                               (entry_credential entrant) is never the entry lane's house spend
//                               (laneSpentSql). A cut-off one retires the house key it holds, if
//                               any: its entry lane held none, its spend the entrant's and unmetered here
//                  entry        an entrant's pass, before it claims its trial, reads the secrets its account
//                  secrets      pushed to the competition (server/secrets/store.ts sealedEntrySecretsFor:
//                               the active rows; none: model-free, above), of the provider lane those of
//                               a provider the allowlist serves alone (a key for another pays for no call:
//                               never opened, never recorded), and opens each with the grader's private
//                               keys (store.ts openEntrySecretRows, server/secrets/seal.ts;
//                               AgentTrialDeps.entrySecrets.seal, default the environment's). A house-paid
//                               entry's pass reads none. No private key here, or a secret it cannot open:
//                               the trial held (ENTRY_SECRETS_UNOPENED_HOLD_REASON) and the admins paged,
//                               the fault the platform's, never masq in its place. Two lanes:
//                                 provider     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY or
//                                              GOOGLE_API_KEY: the forwarder's keys alone (agent.ts
//                                              EntrantKeys, its gateway.json, deleted once it is
//                                              ready), never a sandbox's variable; the entry keeps its
//                                              trial key and base URLs. Each is checked with its
//                                              provider first (gateway/providers.ts checkProviderKey:
//                                              its models list, spending nothing):
//                                   valid        the org and project ids its answers named are masked
//                                                with the keys, the pass runs on the keys, and the
//                                                secrets are marked used, the keys validated (markUsed)
//                                   refused      401, 402 or 403: on the final the pass waits for the
//                                                entrant to push a new key, the run flagged
//                                                ENTRY_SECRET_HELD_FLAG (stage.ts reads it), the key
//                                                checked again every AGENT_PROVIDER_KEY_RECHECK_MS (its
//                                                job sent for the next slot) within
//                                                AGENT_PROVIDER_KEY_HOLD_MS of the first refusal (an
//                                                ENTRY_SECRET_HELD_ACTION audit row: the window's start
//                                                and end), capped at the final phase's end; past it (or
//                                                once the competition is resolved, or on the dev phase
//                                                at once) the trial scores 0 (keyRefusedRecord):
//                                                recorded as a timeout, its record a cassette with no
//                                                entry and an empty export, void_reason
//                                                PROVIDER_KEY_REFUSED and the readable why as its
//                                                error, nothing run, nothing spent
//                                   unreachable  no verdict (no connection, the budget out, a 5xx): the
//                                                pass waits and checks again the same way, paged at
//                                                most once an hour, never scored for it: never the
//                                                entrant's
//                                 env          every other name: a variable of the entry's own sandbox
//                                              (agent.ts RunTrialOptions.secrets, SandboxSpec.secrets),
//                                              never the env's, a forwarder's or the scorer's, and the
//                                              same on the pass's replay, which opens exactly the rows
//                                              its live pass recorded (sealedEntrySecretsFor by id). One
//                                              erased meanwhile (replaced or removed by its entrant, or
//                                              purged) voids the live pass (ENTRY_SECRETS_ERASED_VOID_REASON),
//                                              so a fresh one runs on what the entrant holds now:
//                                              a replay on other values would replay nothing
//                               Every form of every value the pass holds (gateway/secret-mask.ts: both
//                               lanes, and the ids learned) is masked out of what it stores and says:
//                               the forwarder's answers and cassette (its `mask`), each request before
//                               the forwarder keys it (its `request_mask`, the env lane's, the replay's
//                               forwarder handed the same), the stored stderr tail, the pass's error, the
//                               words of a refused key's wait or zero and of a cut-off pass, and every
//                               log and page line; no value is stored or logged. The env's export and
//                               call log are scanned after each pass, never masked (they are scored and
//                               replayed byte for byte: agent.ts secretsInPassOutputs): a hit flags the
//                               run SECRET_IN_OUTPUT_FLAG beside a SECRET_IN_OUTPUT_ACTION audit row
//                               naming the secret's NAME and the file, never the value. Each pass, keys
//                               or none, also tells its forwarder whether an entrant can push a secret on
//                               this deployment at all (agent.ts EntrantKeys.entrySecrets, the config's
//                               entry_secrets): `on` while the seal settings hold a public key (the one the
//                               web seals with, from the same environment), `off` without one
//                               (entrySecretSealRefusal `seal`), when the no-key 401 says pushing is not
//                               open here yet instead of naming `makefun secrets push`
//                  spend        no contest-level spend gate: a live pass, dev or final, the first of its trial
//                               or a re-run, starts with no spend weighed on either lane, whatever the bundle
//                               names (inference's and target's dev_daily_usd, dev_total_usd and
//                               max_total_usd are read by nothing here): no day, practice budget or
//                               competition total holds it, and no row is locked to weigh one. What bounds
//                               a pass is its own budget alone: budget_usd_per_trial at the gateway
//                               forwarder, its key's masq cap at that × 1.05 (gateway/masq.ts),
//                               max_requests_per_trial and the per-request caps. A grade-trial job an
//                               earlier release sent for a pass it held back (ids keyed `daily:<day>`,
//                               `total:<day>` and `final-cap:<first>:<slot>`) starts its pass as it wakes,
//                               and a run flag such a release wrote (dev_daily_cap, dev_total_cap,
//                               final_total_cap) is neither written nor taken off here
//                  pricing      a live pass meters both lanes on its run's pricing revision (trialPricingRev:
//                               spend-revision.ts runPricingRev), named as the pass sets out: the one the
//                               cassette of the run's lowest-index recorded trial names, else the receipt's
//                               (submission.pricing_rev, what ingest priced the entry on), so a release that
//                               changes pricing/rows.json mid-run leaves no trial of it on another table.
//                               A revision this grader holds no table of is a PlatformFaultError before
//                               anything is minted or claimed (the trial held, the platform's fault); a
//                               refused key's empty cassettes (keyRefusedRecord) are stamped with it too
//                  house lane   with a target (contracts/competition.ts AgentTarget, metered apart from
//                               the entry's calls), the env's calls to it run on a house key of the
//                               pass's own, on target.budget_usd_per_trial, its spend metered apart
//                               (run_trial house_spend_micro_usd, its cassette's totals, +
//                               voided_house_spend_micro_usd). The pass's mints claim the trial on the
//                               entry's key and record the house's beside it (house_masq_key_id), so a
//                               pass cut off retires both, each lane's meter counted as that lane's
//                               voided spend. An entrant's pass mints the house's alone, which claims
//                               the trial (`entry lane` above). A target whose models are all
//                               superbot-router's house ids (targetOnRouter) has its house lane on the
//                               router instead, never masq: the `router` upstream at
//                               MAKEFUN_SUPERBOT_ROUTER_URL on MAKEFUN_SUPERBOT_ROUTER_HOUSE_KEY, at
//                               MAKEFUN_SUPERBOT_ROUTER_HOUSE_SPEED, its user the pass's house label
//                               (masq.ts trialKeyLabel, role house). Nothing is minted or retired for
//                               that lane (house_masq_key_id stays null; its spend is the cassette's, as
//                               ever), so an entrant's pass claims the trial as it sets out. With no
//                               house key configured, or a target naming a router id beside any other
//                               model, no pass starts: a HouseRouterRefusal, met as a refused key is
//                               (nothing marked, paged once an hour per competition, the job retried)
//                  scrape heat  while a scrape/v1 heat holds this host's lease under the `host` lease
//                               scope (scrapeHostHeldBy: `scrape/v1` below; under `egress` nothing here
//                               waits), a trial's job runs nothing: it hands itself on to
//                               the next recheck slot (SCRAPE_HOST_RECHECK_MS; gradeTrialJobId of the
//                               pass, its series and the slot, at the trial's expiry; one yet to start
//                               its live pass takes a fresh place in the queue as it wakes), so
//                               no pass shares the CPU with a timed heat, none spends its expiry
//                               waiting one out, and nothing waits in a stopping process
//                  node room    on the k8s sandbox the node's pod slots are shared by every namespace (prod,
//                               dev, the races: sandbox/k8s.ts's header, Room on the node). A live pass or a
//                               replay sets out, and a live_done pass is scored, only while the node has
//                               room for its pods beside server/jobs.ts NODE_POD_HEADROOM (AgentTrialDeps
//                               .podRoom: K8sSandbox.nodePodRoom: of each node, its own pod range's
